# Armv9 SVE2 (FEAT_SVE2) and SVE2.1 (FEAT_SVE2p1), with the SVE2 crypto
# extensions (SVE-AES, SVE-AES2, SVE-SHA3, SVE-SM4, SVE-BitPerm) and SVE B16B16.
#
# Generated: the encodings (fixed bits and operand fields) come from LLVM's
# AArch64 TableGen instruction records whose predicates name these features;
# mnemonics, operand order and operand text come from LLVM's disassembler
# (llvm-mc -M no-aliases), field value by field value, so each operand table
# below lists exactly the field values LLVM accepts. Every instruction lifts to
# a user operation named after its mnemonic (SVE2_<mnemonic>) whose output is the
# register it writes (the first register of a register list) and whose inputs
# are its source operands (with the old destination for the destructive and
# accumulating forms). The flag-setting predicate generators (while*) also set
# NZCV from their result through SVE2_sve_first/none/nlast. Element-wise
# semantics depend on the run-time vector length, so they stay inside the user
# operations; the data flow between Z, P and general registers is kept.

define token sv2tok (32) endian = little
